<details id="coverage" class="coverage"><summary>Disclaimer, methodology &amp; sources</summary><h2>Disclaimer &amp; methodology</h2><p>Population, household and literacy colours use linked, published Census 2011 records. District and constituency summaries include verified village links, exclude towns and wards, and are not official area totals. Literacy is weighted by population aged 7+. Unavailable or unverified values appear grey.</p><p>Urban polygons link only to verified existing Census town identities. Census values retain their publication year and original geography; current LGD district links provide navigation, without asserting that boundary editions are equivalent. Original LGD, SOI and Census IDs and polygons are retained.</p><h3>Rainfall · IMD 2023–2024</h3><p>Annual rainfall is an area-weighted estimate from the official 0.25° daily grid intersected with the displayed polygon. It is not a village rain-gauge reading or an official administrative total. District and constituency estimates use their displayed boundaries, independently of Census or JJM coverage. Incomplete daily records, absent IMD cells and areas outside the grid remain unavailable; they are never zero-filled. Coastal and island boundaries can lack complete source coverage. Original LGD, SOI, Census IDs and polygons are unchanged. Source years 2023 and 2024; downloaded 14 October 2026. Two years do not establish a climate normal.</p><p><a href="https://imdpune.gov.in/cmpg/Griddata/Rainfall_25_NetCDF.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Official IMD rainfall source ↗</a> · Pai et al. (2014), MAUSAM 65(1), 1–18. <a href="/maps/imd-rainfall-annual-2023-2024.json">Grid values, original coordinates, dates and source checksums</a>. IMD notes that its data may contain errors or omissions.</p><div id="map-diagnostics"></div><h2>Coverage &amp; gaps</h2><p><strong>{{ number_format($catalogue['audit']['indexed_shapes']) }}</strong> indexed source shapes across <strong>{{ count($catalogue['layers']